1
00:00:07,196 --> 00:00:09,676
What happened?

2
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:10,134
The baby-sitter called.

3
00:00:10,134 --> 00:00:12,905
His daughter is sick.

4
00:00:12,905 --> 00:00:13,899
What's wrong?

5
00:00:13,899 --> 00:00:17,868
I think she has a stomachache.

6
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:20,846
He's a good father.

7
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:26,802
So... what do you think of him?

8
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:28,650
He's very nice.

9
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:31,730
But I think he was nervous tonight.

10
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:33,958
It was his first date in two years.

11
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:37,344
Will you see him again?

12
00:00:37,344 --> 00:00:39,381
I hope so.

13
00:00:39,381 --> 00:00:44,669
This food is delicious.

14
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:50,733
He didn't get a thing to eat.

15
00:00:50,733 --> 00:00:52,125
You ordered enough for three or four people,

16
00:00:52,125 --> 00:00:54,830
but I'm not complaining.

17
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:56,283
The food is delicious.

18
00:00:56,283 --> 00:01:00,059
Who is that?

19
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:02,059
Do you think it's...

20
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:10,733
No. You won't believe it, Marilyn!

21
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:18,427
I believe it. Even without looking.

22
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:18,694
Hi!

23
00:01:18,694 --> 00:01:18,960
How...?

24
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:21,405
Your downstairs neighbor let me in.

25
00:01:21,405 --> 00:01:23,072
Did you go home?

26
00:01:23,072 --> 00:01:25,739
I did , but everything is OK,

27
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:26,961
so I decided to come back.

28
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,339
To apologize for leaving so early,

29
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,067
I brought you a little gift.

30
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:32,317
It's a bonsai tree

31
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:34,317
for your new apartment.

32
00:01:34,317 --> 00:01:36,655
Hi, Marilyn. I hope it's not too late.

33
00:01:36,655 --> 00:01:38,273
Oh, not at all. We're still eating.

34
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:41,251
Please, come in. Join us.

35
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:44,229
It's our meal from the restaurant.

36
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:48,247
And how is your daughter?

37
00:01:48,247 --> 00:01:49,087
Oh, she's fine.

38
00:01:49,087 --> 00:01:50,185
It was only a tummy ache.

39
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,163
It's good that you went back.

40
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,140
Yes, I think it's important for me to be there

41
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,140
since her mother died.

42
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:02,096
I agree. Aren't you hungry?

43
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,074
As a matter of fact... I am hungry.

44
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:08,052
There's lots of food left.

45
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:12,230
Mmm, this is delicious!

46
00:02:12,230 --> 00:02:12,830
Enjoy!

47
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:14,815
I'm going to excuse myself.

48
00:02:14,815 --> 00:02:19,043
I have a lot of work to do to get ready for tomorrow.

49
00:02:19,043 --> 00:02:22,154
Good night, Harry. It was nice meeting you.

50
00:02:22,154 --> 00:02:22,942
Bye, Marilyn.

51
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:23,942
Good night, Susan.

52
00:02:23,942 --> 00:02:25,920
Good night, Marilyn.

53
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:32,205
She's going to a fashion show here in the city tomorrow.

54
00:02:32,205 --> 00:02:32,405
She is sleeping here

55
00:02:32,292 --> 00:02:37,014
so she won't have to travel from Riverdale in the morning.

56
00:02:37,014 --> 00:02:39,592
You two must be close.

57
00:02:39,592 --> 00:02:40,810
we are.

58
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:53,787
The whole Stewart family is close.

59
00:02:53,787 --> 00:02:54,852
I like that.

60
00:02:54,852 --> 00:02:59,964
And then, two years ago, my wife died.

61
00:02:59,964 --> 00:03:01,249
You miss her.

62
00:03:01,249 --> 00:03:07,612
I do...yes, but I have Michelle...

63
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:08,412
and with time...

64
00:03:08,412 --> 00:03:14,234
Is there anyone else in your life?

65
00:03:14,234 --> 00:03:17,745
No, not yet. What about you?

66
00:03:17,745 --> 00:03:18,945
Oh, I date occasionally,

67
00:03:18,945 --> 00:03:22,501
but my work keeps me busy.

68
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:23,734
Ooh, speaking of keeping busy-

69
00:03:23,734 --> 00:03:25,214
I have an early start tomorrow,

70
00:03:25,214 --> 00:03:29,790
and the baby-sitter has to get home.

71
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:37,413
Where did the time go?

72
00:03:37,413 --> 00:03:37,677
It's midnight.

73
00:03:37,677 --> 00:03:38,534
Thank you, Susan.

74
00:03:38,534 --> 00:03:39,891
I had a nice evening.

75
00:03:39,891 --> 00:03:49,303
Me, too, Harry.

76
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:52,281
Harry?

77
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:52,710
Yes?

78
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:55,583
I'd like to meet your daughter someday.

79
00:03:55,583 --> 00:03:58,837
Does that mean that I can see you again?

80
00:03:58,837 --> 00:04:00,037
Of course.

81
00:04:00,037 --> 00:04:01,715
Wonderful. I'll call you,

82
00:04:01,715 --> 00:04:03,215
and we'll go out to dinner.

83
00:04:03,215 --> 00:04:03,715
Please do.

84
00:04:03,715 --> 00:04:06,193
I promise I won't leave early.

85
00:04:06,193 --> 00:04:07,171
It was for a good reason.

86
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:08,947
You know something?

87
00:04:08,947 --> 00:04:09,539
What?

88
00:04:09,539 --> 00:04:12,982
I think we're going to be good friends.

89
00:04:12,982 --> 00:04:15,087
Good night, Susan.

90
00:04:15,087 --> 00:04:16,945
Good night, Harry,

91
00:04:16,945 --> 00:04:18,945
Have a safe trip home.

92
00:04:18,945 --> 00:04:28,016
Are you all right?

93
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:28,683
Sorry.

94
00:04:28,683 --> 00:04:35,472
I never liked that umbrella stand.

95
00:04:35,472 --> 00:04:38,472
Good night, Harry.
